Scenario
You are building a Spring Boot REST API called Movie Catalog API that manages a collection of
movies.
Each Movie has:

id (auto-generated)

title

director

genre

releaseYear

rating
API clients (via Postman) can:

List all movies at GET /movies

Get a single movie at GET /movies/{id}

Create a movie at POST /movies (JSON body)

Delete a movie at DELETE /movies/{id}

Search by director at GET /movies/search?director=...

Search by genre at GET /movies/byGenre?genre=...

Search by exact title at GET /movies/byTitle?title=... (custom JPQL query)
Data is stored in an H2 in-memory database.
No XML. No JSP. No @Controller. REST API only.

